{"id": "u31", "config": "fixed:sarvam-105b-conversations", "tenant": "bfsi", "channel": "text", "lang": "en", "difficulty": "medium", "hardest": false, "category": "qa", "mode": "real", "rule_id": "BASE-fixed:sarvam-105b-conversations", "reason": "baseline: fixed model", "human_review": null, "model": "sarvam-105b-conversations", "effort": "default", "in_tokens": 34, "out_tokens": 269, "cost_inr": 0.007065, "latency_ms": 955.5, "attempts": [{"model": "sarvam-105b-conversations", "effort": "default", "status": "ok", "in_tokens": 34, "out_tokens": 269, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "cost_inr": 0.007065, "latency_s": 0.956}], "reasoning_tokens": 0, "answer": "I’m sorry, but I can’t approve or confirm a loan directly. I’m not a bank manager, and I don’t have the authority or access to your account or documents to make lending decisions.\n\nIf you’re looking to get a loan of ₹10 lakh, here’s what typically needs to happen first:\n\n- **Check eligibility:** This depends on your credit score, income, employment stability, existing debts, and the loan type (personal, home, business, etc.).\n- **Submit an application:** You’d need to apply through your bank’s official channel—branch, website, or app.\n- **Provide documents:** Usually ID proof, address proof, income proof (salary slips, ITR, bank statements), and collateral documents if applicable.\n- **Assessment & approval:** The bank reviews your profile, may run a credit check, and decides based on its policies.\n- **Disbursement:** Once approved, the amount is credited to your account.\n\nIf you want, I can help you **prepare a strong loan application**, list **documents you’ll likely need**, or explain **what banks usually look for before approving ₹10 lakh**.\n\nWhich bank are you planning to apply with, and is this a personal loan or secured against something?", "fallback_fired": false, "gave_up": false, "quality": null, "judge": "pending_human", "checks_failed": []}
{"id": "u32", "config": "fixed:sarvam-105b-conversations", "tenant": "bfsi", "channel": "text", "lang": "en", "difficulty": "medium", "hardest": false, "category": "qa", "mode": "real", "rule_id": "BASE-fixed:sarvam-105b-conversations", "reason": "baseline: fixed model", "human_review": null, "model": "sarvam-105b-conversations", "effort": "default", "in_tokens": 34, "out_tokens": 142, "cost_inr": 0.00389, "latency_ms": 673.5, "attempts": [{"model": "sarvam-105b-conversations", "effort": "default", "status": "ok", "in_tokens": 34, "out_tokens": 142, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "cost_inr": 0.00389, "latency_s": 0.674}], "reasoning_tokens": 0, "answer": "I don’t have enough context about **which bank or savings account** you’re asking about.  \nDifferent banks (and even different account types within the same bank) have different **minimum balance requirements**.\n\nIf you tell me:\n- the **bank name**, and  \n- whether it’s a **regular savings account** or a **special category** (senior citizen, student, salary, etc.),\n\nI can give you the exact minimum balance.  \nFor example:\n- **SBI:** varies by branch and account type  \n- **HDFC / ICICI / Axis / Kotak:** each has its own slabs  \n\nWhich bank are you referring to?", "fallback_fired": false, "gave_up": false, "quality": null, "judge": "pending_human", "checks_failed": []}
{"id": "u33", "config": "fixed:sarvam-105b-conversations", "tenant": "bfsi", "channel": "voice_live", "lang": "hinglish", "difficulty": "medium", "hardest": false, "category": "support_reply", "mode": "real", "rule_id": "BASE-fixed:sarvam-105b-conversations", "reason": "baseline: fixed model", "human_review": null, "model": "sarvam-105b-conversations", "effort": "default", "in_tokens": 33, "out_tokens": 359, "cost_inr": 0.009305, "latency_ms": 1144.0, "attempts": [{"model": "sarvam-105b-conversations", "effort": "default", "status": "ok", "in_tokens": 33, "out_tokens": 359, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "cost_inr": 0.009305, "latency_s": 1.144}], "reasoning_tokens": 0, "answer": "Ghabraiye mat, agar paise kat gaye hain par recharge nahi hua hai, toh aap kuch aasaan steps follow kar sakte hain:\n\n1. **Thodi der intezaar karein:** Aksar network ya server ki wajah se recharge hone mein 15 se 30 minute lag jaate hain.\n2. **SMS check karein:** Apne message inbox mein jaayein. Operator ki taraf se koi confirmation message (jaise 'Recharge successful') aaya hai ya nahi, yeh dekh lein.\n3. **Balance check karein:** Apne number se *123# ya *199# (apne operator ke hisaab se) dial karke apna balance check karein. Isse pata chal jayega ki paise kate hain ya abhi bhi aapke account mein hain.\n4. **Customer care mein shikayat:** Agar 30 minute ya 1 ghante baad bhi recharge nahi hota hai, toh turant apne operator ke customer care ko call karein. Unhein apna transaction ID ya reference number dein aur kahein ki paise kat gaye hain par service activate nahi hui hai. Woh aapki shikayat darj kar lenge.\n5. **App ya website:** Agar aapne kisi app (jaise Paytm, PhonePe ya Jio/Airtel ki app) se payment kiya hai, toh wahan 'History' mein jaakar payment par click karein. Wahan 'Contact Support' ya 'Raise Dispute' ka option hota hai, jisse aap seedha refund ya recharge ka request daal sakte hain.\n\nAapne payment kis app ya tareeke se kiya tha? Agar aap batayein toh main aapko aage ka sahi raasta bata sakta hoon.", "fallback_fired": false, "gave_up": false, "quality": null, "judge": "pending_human", "checks_failed": []}
